// wdoc section: Diagrams.
page wdoc_diagrams { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Diagrams"

  p "A `diagram` block holds SVG shapes. Coordinates are free-form by default; auto-layout, connection routing, and optional pan + zoom are layered on top via flags on the block."

  h2 "The diagram block"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Field" | "Meaning" |
      | "`width` / `height`"  | "Diagram canvas size in pixels" |
      | "`layout`"            | "`:free` (default) or `:layered` — see Flowcharts" |
      | "`layer_gap`"         | "Spacing between layers when `layout = :layered`" |
      | "`pan_zoom`"          | "When `true`, wrap in an interactive viewport with `+`/`−`/`⟲` controls" |
      | "`zoom_min` / `zoom_max`" | "Scale clamps for pan/zoom" |
      | "`pan_margin`"        | "Overscroll px beyond the content bounds (pan/zoom)" |
  }

  h2 "Primitive shapes"

  p "`rect`, `circle`, `line`, `polygon`, `path`, `label`, `image`, and `container` are the core primitives. Each carries position, size, and paint fields (`fill`, `stroke`, …)."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width  = 280
  height = 130

  rect    { x = 10.0  y = 10.0  width = 60.0  height = 60.0  fill = "#cce" }
  circle  { cx = 120.0  cy = 40.0  r = 24.0  stroke = "black" }
  line    { x1 = 0.0  y1 = 40.0  x2 = 280.0  y2 = 40.0  stroke = "#888" }
  polygon { points = "180,10 230,40 180,70"  fill = "#fc8" }
  label "halfway" { x = 110.0  y = 76.0 }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Connections"

  p "Inside a `diagram`, `source -> destination :kind` draws an edge between two shapes (matched by `id`). The optional `:kind` tag is a symbol; the renderer routes the edge based on the diagram's layout."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width = 320  height = 120
  rect { id = a  x = 10.0   y = 10.0  width = 60.0  height = 40.0 }
  rect { id = b  x = 200.0  y = 10.0  width = 60.0  height = 40.0 }

  a -> b
  a -> b :flow
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Pan & zoom"

  p "Set `pan_zoom = true` to wrap the diagram in an interactive viewport. Wheel zooms toward the cursor, drag pans, the corner buttons zoom about centre / reset. Zoom is clamped to `[zoom_min, zoom_max]`; pan allows half-a-viewport of overscroll past each content edge plus the author's `pan_margin`."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
diagram {
  width = 600  height = 400  pan_zoom = true
  zoom_min = 0.5  zoom_max = 4.0
  // … shapes …
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Player asset" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "The bundled diagram-pan-zoom.js is auto-included only on pages that use pan_zoom = true, mirroring the terminal-player and dopesheet-player asset pattern."
  }

  p "Next: [Flowcharts](wdoc_flowcharts)."
}
